### Competitor & Factual Source Verification

* **Competitor URL:** Blank in source row (not invented). Market intent was evaluated across leading Indian fine jewellers (CaratLane, Tanishq, Malabar) to identify critical buyer considerations: desk ergonomics, laptop typing clearance, clasp redundancy, and dent prevention.
* **Factual Sources & Regulations:**
  1. **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS):** Mandatory 3-mark hallmarking for gold jewellery (BIS triangle stamp, karatage/fineness stamp e.g. 18K750 / 22K916, and laser-etched 6-digit alphanumeric HUID). Digital authentication verified via the official BIS CARE mobile application.
  2. **Indian Taxation Law:** Mandatory 3% Goods and Services Tax (GST) applied to the combined value of bullion and making charges.
  3. **Metallurgical Hardness Standards:** 18K gold (140–160 HV) versus 22K gold (60–80 HV) tensile strength, explaining why 18K is optimal for slender daily bangles and diamond settings while 22K suits classic solid round bangles.

